# Session History

## 2026-04-12 - Recovery Planning and Implementation

### Regressions Observed
- Codeblocks lost readability because syntax-highlighted block code was inheriting inline-code styling, which also introduced visible gutter artifacts and misaligned line numbers.
- Media assets did not expose the required hover control panel, and the inline-to-modal animation was too abrupt to feel intentional.
- Mermaid and Graphviz diagrams lacked modal navigation controls for pan, zoom, reset, and reload.
- URL extraction failed with `Not Found` because the frontend assumed a single extractor path that did not match the local runtime.

### Repo and Runtime Findings
- `MdxCodeblock` was rendering with `PreTag="div"`, which allowed `.markdown-content :not(pre) > code` to leak into block code.
- `MediaAssetFrame` only rendered a single zoom button and used Motion shared-layout transitions for a portal-based modal flow.
- Mermaid and Graphviz previews produced SVG output without a dedicated viewport controller for drag/pan/zoom.
- A non-sidecar service was listening on port `8787`, returning `Cannot GET /health` and `Cannot POST /extract`; the URL extractor sidecar had to be started on `8788`.
- `codebase-retrieval` was unavailable in this environment with `401 Unauthorized`.

### Architecture Decisions
- Keep Radix Dialog for modal semantics and accessibility.
- Use GSAP-based transform/opacity choreography for media open/close rather than continuing with Motion shared-layout.
- Use `@panzoom/panzoom` for modal Mermaid/Graphviz viewport controls.
- Keep codeblocks visually minimal: one dark surface, transparent actions, no nested outlines or stray gutter backgrounds.
- Add extractor endpoint probing with fallback to `VITE_MDE_URL_SIDECAR_ORIGIN` or a direct local sidecar origin.

